01:35:09.440 --> 01:35:11.180
With a restricted plate, that's

01:35:11.180 --> 01:35:12.780
not very easy because you can

01:35:12.780 --> 01:35:15.590
only gain inches at a time.

01:35:15.590 --> 01:35:17.170
Ken Schrader sits up right

01:35:17.170 --> 01:35:19.430
behind Carson.

01:35:19.430 --> 01:35:20.890
With that restrictor plate, the

01:35:20.890 --> 01:35:23.090
script would have been that one

01:35:23.090 --> 01:35:24.840
waits until the absolute last

01:35:24.840 --> 01:35:26.200
moment, the last corner of the

01:35:26.200 --> 01:35:27.700
last lap, and then darts out of

01:35:27.700 --> 01:35:28.900
the draft and moves past the

01:35:28.900 --> 01:35:30.000
car in front of him.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:31.580
You don't have that kind of power anymore,

01:35:31.700 --> 01:35:33.640
so you've got to get up and get into position early

01:35:33.640 --> 01:35:34.960
and decide where you're going to make your role.

01:35:34.960 --> 01:35:38.380
I think that's why, Paul, we've seen Bill Elliott make his moves.

01:35:38.640 --> 01:35:41.440
He might have done the right thing in just making the moves,

01:35:41.540 --> 01:35:43.730
getting to the front, taking advantage

01:35:43.730 --> 01:35:46.830
while everyone else was kind of thinking about what they were going to do.

01:35:46.830 --> 01:35:49.010
He moved out there and he might still be there.

01:35:49.590 --> 01:35:52.470
Bill Elliott wins this year.

01:35:52.920 --> 01:35:54.870
Looking for a win here in the firecracker.

01:35:55.010 --> 01:35:56.070
Two wins at Daytona.

01:35:56.530 --> 01:35:59.080
25 in his history with the Winston Cup.

01:35:59.440 --> 01:36:00.000
and keep in mind,

01:36:00.410 --> 01:36:02.870
Rusty Wallace still runs back in mid-pack,

01:36:02.870 --> 01:36:05.510
but still has the points lead at this point.

01:36:05.510 --> 01:36:07.150
Dale Earnhardt would love to get up

01:36:07.150 --> 01:36:08.210
into the front of the field.

01:36:08.210 --> 01:36:09.720
Wallace is 14th.

01:36:09.720 --> 01:36:12.960
Earnhardt is running in third place right now,

01:36:12.960 --> 01:36:15.660
and whoever has the most points among those two men

01:36:15.660 --> 01:36:17.220
at the conclusion of this race

01:36:17.220 --> 01:36:20.470
will be $150,000 richer.

01:36:20.470 --> 01:36:23.610
Bill Elliott, number nine, is Ford out in front.

01:36:23.610 --> 01:36:26.050
Rick Wilson, the Oldsmobile, runs in second.

01:36:26.050 --> 01:36:28.550
Earnhardt, a Chevrolet, runs in third,

01:36:28.550 --> 01:36:29.830
and there you see Waltrip.

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:32.200
and other Chevy's that he jumped back and forth.

01:36:32.200 --> 01:36:35.480
Bill Parsons has stopped his attack on Waltrip.

01:36:35.480 --> 01:36:37.330
He's kind of moved into the line,

01:36:37.330 --> 01:36:39.270
waiting to see what will develop,

01:36:39.270 --> 01:36:41.170
because, like I say, at this point,

01:36:41.170 --> 01:36:44.070
inches is all you can gain with the restricted plate.

01:36:44.070 --> 01:36:45.810
The car, it's very exasperating,

01:36:45.810 --> 01:36:48.660
'cause he's set out there, running in that line.

01:36:48.660 --> 01:36:50.360
You've got to wait for the right moment,

01:36:50.360 --> 01:36:52.660
wait 'til someone slips or something happens

01:36:52.660 --> 01:36:54.500
to start a chain reaction down the line

01:36:54.500 --> 01:36:56.600
'cause where the guy just cracks the throttle back,

01:36:56.600 --> 01:36:58.220
when he does, you can take advantage of him.

01:36:58.220 --> 01:37:00.000
But right now that is a

01:37:00.670 --> 01:37:01.830
tell you what on board that

01:37:01.830 --> 01:37:03.650
second place car Rick Wilson has

01:37:03.650 --> 01:37:05.250
to be a very happy man at the

01:37:05.250 --> 01:37:06.670
moment despite the fact that he's

01:37:06.670 --> 01:37:08.510
not in the lead he is in striking

01:37:08.510 --> 01:37:11.420
position and he has never been

01:37:11.420 --> 01:37:13.320
this far up toward the end of a

01:37:13.320 --> 01:37:15.220
race his best finish has been

01:37:15.220 --> 01:37:17.360
seven three times now with ten

01:37:17.360 --> 01:37:18.840
laps to go he's sitting there in

01:37:18.840 --> 01:37:20.950
second place he's got to be happy

01:37:20.950 --> 01:37:22.650
with his position but the key

01:37:22.650 --> 01:37:24.490
position at this race is of

01:37:24.490 --> 01:37:26.290
course Bill Elliott number nine

01:37:26.290 --> 01:37:28.350
out in front Wilson is second

01:37:28.350 --> 01:37:30.000
Earnhardt is third he'll be

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:32.560
We'll be back with more after this.

01:41:48.780 --> 01:41:54.920
just over to go now they come across the stripe four laps to the finish of this 400 mile run

01:41:54.920 --> 01:42:00.000
in first is Bill Elliott Rick Wilson sits in second Dale Earnhardt and then Darrell Waltrip

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:05.520
But Earnhardt and Waldrop are taking a hard look at how to get past the first two place cars.

01:42:05.820 --> 01:42:07.920
And they're hooked up and they've been working together.

01:42:08.300 --> 01:42:10.800
Yes, we've seen Elliott move down low to the bottom.

01:42:11.580 --> 01:42:13.620
And Waldrop move in right behind him.

01:42:13.700 --> 01:42:17.310
So they may be thinking of the draft situation to try to push each other,

01:42:17.430 --> 01:42:21.670
take each other by the lead two cars, which is going to be a tough job.

01:42:21.730 --> 01:42:26.910
Because Elliott is certainly showing more than he has all weekend as far as practice and qualifying.

01:42:27.300 --> 01:42:30.000
Came from 38 starting spot and is now leading this.

01:42:30.000 --> 01:42:31.940
thing, and Rick Wilson is putting his best

01:42:31.940 --> 01:42:33.860
ever show together. Earnhardt's tried

01:42:33.860 --> 01:42:35.880
that through several times in the past few

01:42:35.880 --> 01:42:37.640
laps, where he drops out of the line

01:42:37.640 --> 01:42:39.840
all the way down to the low side. Johnny,

01:42:39.900 --> 01:42:41.840
is he testing to see what he can do on

01:42:41.840 --> 01:42:43.900
perhaps the last lap? I think he wants to

01:42:43.900 --> 01:42:45.900
see if his car will stick down there, and he's

01:42:45.900 --> 01:42:47.700
showing Waltrip that it will, so he

01:42:47.700 --> 01:42:50.140
may be issuing an invitation

01:42:50.140 --> 01:42:52.120
to Darrell, come on, let's see if we can go by

01:42:52.120 --> 01:42:54.000
these guys. It'll bear watching.

01:42:54.280 --> 01:42:55.970
That's Bill Parsons, the number 55

01:42:55.970 --> 01:42:58.050
car that runs in fifth place right now.

01:42:58.350 --> 01:43:00.000
Rick Wilson is glued right on the

01:43:00.000 --> 01:43:01.720
Back bumper of the leader, Bill Elliott.

01:43:02.100 --> 01:43:05.880
Wilson, with 10 laps to go last year, was in this position, second place,

01:43:05.960 --> 01:43:09.120
but then crashes in the final lap, took Wilson out of the running.

01:43:09.240 --> 01:43:13.440
I'm sure that's going through his mind as well as he chases Bill Elliott against.

01:43:13.860 --> 01:43:18.600
Dale Earnhardt comes down on the inside and takes a look at running in the low groove.

01:43:18.600 --> 01:43:23.770
We can see Darryl has dropped back a little bit there, but I don't think it's any problem.

01:43:24.030 --> 01:43:27.070
He's just kind of coasting, seeing where he'll fit in.

01:43:27.440 --> 01:43:29.280
They may be getting ready to make their move.

01:43:29.340 --> 01:43:30.000
They're going to have to do

01:43:30.000 --> 01:43:31.780
something here if they're going to pretty quick.

01:43:32.200 --> 01:43:33.940
Four times in history the lead

01:43:33.940 --> 01:43:35.940
has changed on the last lap

01:43:35.940 --> 01:43:37.920
at the firecracker. Will it happen

01:43:37.920 --> 01:43:40.060
again this year? Elliott has

01:43:40.060 --> 01:43:41.810
run a good race

01:43:41.810 --> 01:43:43.930
and of course he has victories here

01:43:43.930 --> 01:43:45.910
on this track. So Paul Elliott out in

01:43:45.910 --> 01:43:47.530
front with the help of Rick Wilson.

01:43:48.050 --> 01:43:49.990
Elliott started 38

01:43:49.990 --> 01:43:51.990
now runs in first place

01:43:51.990 --> 01:43:53.950
and is he looking at a win

01:43:53.950 --> 01:43:55.150
in the firecracker?

01:43:55.510 --> 01:43:57.580
The spoiler could be the combination of

01:43:57.580 --> 01:43:59.450
Earnhardt and Waldrop as here comes

01:43:59.450 --> 01:44:00.000
Arnold.

01:44:00.410 --> 01:44:04.150
In third place, car number three, down on the inside once again.

01:44:04.150 --> 01:44:09.260
And again, Waltrip lays back just a bit and stays out of that pull.

01:44:09.260 --> 01:44:13.620
Out in front, Rick Wilson, look at him, he maneuvers right behind Bill Elliott.

01:44:13.620 --> 01:44:16.280
I think he's going to have to stay right there if he has a chance.

01:44:16.280 --> 01:44:20.860
White flag is out, one more lap, so now's the time, the last lap.

01:44:20.860 --> 01:44:23.850
If anybody's going to do anything, this is when it'll happen.

01:44:23.850 --> 01:44:25.090
The guesswork is over.

01:44:25.090 --> 01:44:30.000
Wilson moves down out of his more familiar position of directly behind Elliott.

01:44:30.030 --> 01:44:31.270
It drives a little bit on the

01:44:31.270 --> 01:44:31.830
low side.

01:44:32.190 --> 01:44:33.730
Remember too that depending on

01:44:33.730 --> 01:44:34.910
where they place their car

01:44:34.910 --> 01:44:36.570
relative the car in front of

01:44:36.570 --> 01:44:38.870
them then they can actually

01:44:38.870 --> 01:44:40.210
affect the handling of that

01:44:40.210 --> 01:44:41.210
car in front of them by

01:44:41.210 --> 01:44:42.710
scrolling the way air is coming

01:44:42.710 --> 01:44:43.810
off the back of the car.

01:44:44.050 --> 01:44:44.970
But look at Earnhardt.

01:44:45.220 --> 01:44:46.720
Earnhardt closes up behind

01:44:46.720 --> 01:44:48.020
Wilson and then has to fall

01:44:48.020 --> 01:44:49.920
back as Wilson makes his move

01:44:49.920 --> 01:44:51.000
down to the inside.

01:44:51.260 --> 01:44:53.060
He is alongside Bill Elliott.

01:44:53.300 --> 01:44:55.500
Wilson alongside pushes a nose

01:44:55.500 --> 01:44:56.200
just ahead.

01:44:56.400 --> 01:44:57.840
Will this be the first victory

01:44:57.840 --> 01:44:58.400
for Wilson.

01:44:58.700 --> 01:45:00.000
Elliott is alongside now.

01:45:00.570 --> 01:45:06.530
And Elliott with a nose just ahead of Wilson at the line as they touch.

01:45:06.530 --> 01:45:14.100
Coming across to finish this race, Elliott wins the firecracker with Wilson in second

01:45:14.100 --> 01:45:15.100
place by inches.

01:45:15.100 --> 01:45:17.800
Well, there was experience against you.

01:45:17.800 --> 01:45:23.210
I saw Rick Wilson make his move, he did it a little bit soon, and Elliott still had the

01:45:23.210 --> 01:45:27.940
momentum he knew to be able to come up on the outside and pick him up by just a couple

01:45:27.940 --> 01:45:28.940
of feet at the finish line.

01:45:28.940 --> 01:45:30.000
What a minute.

01:45:30.060 --> 01:45:34.640
and the crew i think somewhat uncertain as to how the finish actually occurred

01:45:35.100 --> 01:45:40.080
but it was bill elliott out in front of rick wilson earnhardt finishes in third

01:46:31.400 --> 01:46:33.550
Bill Parsons die, two of them.

01:46:33.550 --> 01:46:56.050
We got to touch them.

01:46:56.050 --> 01:46:57.940
Finish third, that's two third places.

01:47:00.000 --> 01:47:02.300
Two-thirds places for Phil Parsons this year.

01:47:02.300 --> 01:47:03.620
Yeah, how are the two total?

01:47:03.620 --> 01:47:04.760
Absolutely.

01:47:33.610 --> 01:47:34.970
Let's take a look at the finish

01:47:34.970 --> 01:47:36.710
one more time here that is Rick

01:47:36.710 --> 01:47:38.910
Wilson on the inside to the right

01:47:38.910 --> 01:47:40.950
and Bill Elliott to the outside

01:47:40.950 --> 01:47:42.590
coming to the line Wilson had it

01:47:42.590 --> 01:47:44.450
and Elliott just inched ahead at

01:47:44.450 --> 01:47:46.030
the line at the same time

01:47:46.030 --> 01:47:47.990
Parsons won the three way battle

01:47:47.990 --> 01:47:49.150
for third place.

01:47:49.150 --> 01:47:50.830
Now let's go to winner's circle

01:47:50.830 --> 01:47:52.070
to talk with Bill Elliott.

01:47:52.070 --> 01:47:59.890
Here's Jack a root.

01:48:01.310 --> 01:48:12.560
Well, Bill Elliott, you came from the back of the pack, but you had to stave off Rick

01:48:12.560 --> 01:48:13.560
Wilson.

01:48:13.560 --> 01:48:14.560
A lot of yellow paint on the car in that last lap.

01:48:14.560 --> 01:48:19.220
Well, it got pretty hairy there at the end, but I knew he'd be the car to beat because

01:48:19.220 --> 01:48:20.820
with him behind me, I could run pretty good.

01:48:20.820 --> 01:48:24.120
The only thing he did, he made his move a little bit too early and he didn't get a good

01:48:24.120 --> 01:48:25.130
enough run and go.

01:48:25.130 --> 01:48:26.130
But still, he almost beat me.

01:48:26.130 --> 01:48:30.000
If a finish line had been on at the exit of the trial, he'd have beat me.

01:48:30.380 --> 01:48:32.540
You know that's the way it goes that the car just picked up

01:48:32.540 --> 01:48:35.520
enough to pull back past him and he wasn't able to pick it

01:48:35.520 --> 01:48:36.460
back up quick enough.

01:48:36.460 --> 01:48:38.380
Hard work all day or did you have a feeling that you were

01:48:38.380 --> 01:48:40.960
going to be able to take this one home?

01:48:40.960 --> 01:48:42.300
About a hundred laps in the race.

01:48:42.300 --> 01:48:45.690
I had no idea because I was almost a lap down.

01:48:45.690 --> 01:48:47.570
We blistered one tire.

01:48:47.570 --> 01:48:50.530
It seemed like what started out bad got worse.

01:48:50.530 --> 01:48:53.470
But then the last 50 laps, it just got better and better.

01:48:53.470 --> 01:48:55.730
When the four car got behind me and we saw we could run

01:48:55.730 --> 01:48:58.030
quick together, you know, then he helped me.

01:48:58.030 --> 01:48:58.960
That's all there was to it.

01:48:58.960 --> 01:49:00.000
He helped me to get to where I'm

01:49:00.480 --> 01:49:03.020
Well, Jerry punches with the other combatant on that last lap.

01:49:03.020 --> 01:49:04.000
Jerry?

01:49:04.000 --> 01:49:06.400
Well, red paint on the side of this Oldsmobile for Rick Wilson,

01:49:06.400 --> 01:49:08.100
the hometown driver from nearby Bartow.

01:49:08.100 --> 01:49:10.420
And Rick, did you make the move a little bit too early?

01:49:10.420 --> 01:49:11.260
Well, I might have to.

01:49:11.260 --> 01:49:12.900
You know, the car was running awful good.

01:49:12.900 --> 01:49:14.960
Bill couldn't run a leg by itself, but I could run.

01:49:14.960 --> 01:49:17.550
With me and him hooked together, we could run real good.

01:49:17.550 --> 01:49:19.690
I just waited and waited the last lap, and I thought I'd made it,

01:49:19.690 --> 01:49:20.990
but I thought Earnhardt was going to go with me.

01:49:20.990 --> 01:49:22.010
That was my big mistake there.

01:49:22.010 --> 01:49:24.150
He's been going to the bottom, going to the bottom.

01:49:24.150 --> 01:49:26.150
And I thought he would go, and if he did, I could have beat him.

01:49:26.150 --> 01:49:28.790
And I pulled up beside him until he got close to the finish line.

01:49:28.790 --> 01:49:29.760
I thought I had him.

01:49:30.120 --> 01:49:31.940
four just started pulling. But I want to say the Kodak

01:49:31.940 --> 01:49:34.120
team got a great job today. They kept

01:49:34.120 --> 01:49:36.080
me up front. The car worked great. And this is

01:49:36.080 --> 01:49:38.040
our best finish. And just thank the Lord for a safe race.

01:49:38.790 --> 01:49:40.230
Rick Wilson finishing second here

01:49:40.230 --> 01:49:55.700
at Daytona. It's not as much fun

01:49:55.700 --> 01:49:57.480
to come to Daytona in a race as it used to be.

01:49:59.660 --> 01:50:00.000
Restricting

01:50:00.350 --> 01:50:06.980
too much controversy in them they're you know some people maybe getting by with something maybe not

01:50:06.980 --> 01:50:11.600
NASCAR says they're not but you know there's always room to cheat there or let somebody buy

01:50:11.600 --> 01:50:15.440
with something if they're all racing the same thing open competition type thing on the motors

01:50:15.440 --> 01:50:21.850
it'd be hard to cheat except we've got the best motor to run so you know I'm really not for the

01:50:21.850 --> 01:50:30.000
restricted play there's not no fun racing the cars with them on our team. His 26th

01:50:30.000 --> 01:50:33.880
Winston Cup race, followed by Wilson, Parsons, Earnhardt, and Waltrip.

01:50:34.560 --> 01:50:42.540
There were 21 different lead changes among nine different drivers and three cautions for 17 laps.

01:50:42.860 --> 01:50:49.440
Dale Earnhardt actually led the most laps, 52, but Bill Elliott was in front at the finish of the race,

01:50:49.560 --> 01:50:51.180
followed by Rick Wilson.

01:50:54.320 --> 01:51:00.000
And Rusty Wallace wins the $150,000 at the midway.

01:51:00.000 --> 01:51:03.940
Mid-season Winston Cup bonus winner by finishing 12.

01:51:04.920 --> 01:51:09.300
So it is Bill Elliott that is the winner of the day at the Firecracker 400.

01:51:09.620 --> 01:51:11.320
Now let's send you back to Frank Gifford.
